    {
      "id": "e83",
      "name": "2007 BMW X3 LCI",
      "story": [
        "I did more work on this car than any other vehicle I ever owned in my life. There were a lot of firsts - first clutch replacement, first SUV, first backup camera, etc. I actually created a detailed build log on <a href=\"https://www.bimmerfest.com/threads/some-pictures-of-my-2007-x3-and-a-short-story.1450887/\">Bimmerfest</a>.",
        "This was a really rare spec - an LCI with the N52 engine and a 6-speed manual transmission in a beautiful highland green metallic. I think this is my favorite color out of any vehicle I owned.",
        "I made many modifications to this, but my favorite was retrofitting heated sports seats. They were in like-new condition and were some of the most comfortable seats I've ever sat in.",
        "I sold this once I went all-EV, but it was really cool. I drove this all over the place - Boston, NYC multiple times, Pittsburgh, and on and on.",
        "I learned so much about working on vehicles from owning this."
      ],
