    {
      "id": "saturn",
      "name": "2000 Saturn SW2",
      "story": [
        "The car that would not die! I bought this for $1900, drove it for six years, longer than any other car I've owned, and sold it for $2400. It was easy to repair, it had a light clutch and decent shifter, it had a lot of room for such a small car, it was great in the snow, parts for it were super cheap... I could go on. This is the car I miss the most out of all the ones I sold. I mean, it was a brown, manual transmission wagon. What more could you ask for!"
      ],
