    {
      "id": "e60",
      "name": "2004 BMW 545i",
      "story": [
        "My first BMW. What an amazing engine, until you had to work on it. What an amazing interior. The seats were 18-way adjustable and simply exceptionally comfortable. This was the best handling car I ever owned. Ultimately, I hated working on it. The engine bay was really meant for a straight 6. It had a lot of common problems, and repairs were always just a nightmare, and I was no stranger to working on German cars! I also never liked the styling. I loved the driving experience, but I was glad to see it go."
      ],
      "cover": "assets/photos/cars/e60/thumb/pictures-1.jpg",
