    {
      "id": "v70",
      "name": "2007 Volvo V70",
      "story": [
        "What a strange car. I always wanted a Volvo wagon. I got this one for an amazing price, as the dealer thought it had a transmission problem, but it just had a faulty brake pressure sensor and fuel pressure sensor. It was about $120 for those sensors and maybe another $300 to change the timing belt and some other miscellaneous items. The color was a beautiful Barents Blue and the interior cleaned up wonderfully. It had an absurd amount of trunk space.",
        "However, I ended up not liking the driving experience at all. The turbo 5 was too torquey and would spin the front wheels very easily. This also made it not great in the snow, even with Blizzaks. The killer was the seats though. They were the most uncomfortable seats I've ever experienced in my life and left me in excruciating pain if I drove for more than an hour.",
        "I only owned this for 6 months. I never wanted to like a car so much, but it ended up just not being for me."
      ],
